zes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"generally between ±0.001\" and ±0.002\" is possible for zinc","note":"derived: the looser end, 0.002 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumWallMinMM","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumWallMinMM","value":0.9,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s least wall","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Aluminum alloys — Min. Thickness 0.9 mm (0.035 in)"}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumWallRecMM","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumWallRecMM","value":2,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s typical wall","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/die-casting-design-faq","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Wall thickness, typically is 2mm for aluminum die casting."}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumDraftMinDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumDraftMinDeg","value":0.5,"unit":"deg","description":"an aluminium alloy’s least draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Aluminum alloys — Min. Draft Angle 0.5º"}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumDr