.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Aluminum alloys — Min. Thickness 0.9 mm (0.035 in)"}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumWallRecMM","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumWallRecMM","value":2,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s typical wall","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/die-casting-design-faq","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Wall thickness, typically is 2mm for aluminum die casting."}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumDraftMinDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumDraftMinDeg","value":0.5,"unit":"deg","description":"an aluminium alloy’s least draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Aluminum alloys — Min. Draft Angle 0.5º"}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumDraftRecDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumDraftRecDeg","value":1,"unit":"deg","description":"an aluminium alloy’s draft, achievable in general (the low end of 1º–2º)","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"For draft angles, in general, 0.5º is achievable for zinc 1º-2º is achievable for aluminum."}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumTolMM","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumTolMM","value":0.1016,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s linear tolerance, ±","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"aluminum can hold between ±0.002\" and ±0.004\"","note":"derived: the looser end, 0.004 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"die-casting.copperWallMinMM","process":"die-casting","key":"copperWallMinMM","value":1.25,"unit":"mm","description":"a copper alloy’s (brass’s) least wall","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Copper alloys (Brass) — Min. Thickness 1.25 mm (0.050 in)"}},{"id":"die-casting.copperDraftMinDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"copperDraftMinDeg","value":0.7,"unit":"deg","description":"a copper alloy’s (brass’s) least draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Copper alloys (Brass) — Min. Draft Angle 0.7º"}},{"id":"sand-casting.aluminiumWallMinMM","process":"sand-casting","key":"aluminiumWallMinMM","value":2.54,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s least wall or web","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read of