e value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Zinc alloys — Min. Thickness 0.6 mm (0.025 in)"}},{"id":"die-casting.zincDraftMinDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"zincDraftMinDeg","value":0.25,"unit":"deg","description":"a zinc alloy’s least draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Zinc alloys — Min. Draft Angle 0.25º"}},{"id":"die-casting.zincDraftRecDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"zincDraftRecDeg","value":0.5,"unit":"deg","description":"a zinc alloy’s draft, achievable in general","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"For draft angles, in general, 0.5º is achievable for zinc 1º-2º is achievable for aluminum."}},{"id":"die-casting.zincTolMM","process":"die-casting","key":"zincTolMM","value":0.0508,"unit":"mm","description":"a zinc alloy’s linear tolerance, ±","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"generally between ±0.001\" and ±0.002\" is possible for zinc","note":"derived: the looser end, 0.002 in × 2