e names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"For draft angles, in general, 0.5º is achievable for zinc 1º-2º is achievable for aluminum."}},{"id":"die-casting.aluminiumTolMM","process":"die-casting","key":"aluminiumTolMM","value":0.1016,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s linear tolerance, ±","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.dynacast.com/resources/article/a-beginners-guide-to-die-cast-design","read":"2026-10-21","label":"aluminum can hold between ±0.002\" and ±0.004\"","note":"derived: the looser end, 0.004 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"die-casting.copperWallMinMM","process":"die-casting","key":"copperWallMinMM","value":1.25,"unit":"mm","description":"a copper alloy’s (brass’s) least wall","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Copper alloys (Brass) — Min. Thickness 1.25 mm (0.050 in)"}},{"id":"die-casting.copperDraftMinDeg","process":"die-casting","key":"copperDraftMinDeg","value":0.7,"unit":"deg","description":"a copper alloy’s (brass’s) least draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.efunda.com/processes/metal_processing/die_casting.cfm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Copper alloys (Brass) — Min. Draft Angle 0.7º"}},{"id":"sand-casting.aluminiumWallMinMM","process":"sand-casting","key":"aluminiumWallMinMM","value":2.54,"unit":"mm","description":"an aluminium alloy’s least wall or web","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"In general web or wall thickness should as a minimum be 0.10\" - Aluminum, .13 Magnesium and .13 for Steel.","note":"derived: 0.10 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"sand-casting.magnesiumWallMinMM","process":"sand-casting","key":"magnesiumWallMinMM","value":3.302,"unit":"mm","description":"a magnesium alloy’s least wall or web","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"In general web or wall thickness should as a minimum be 0.10\" - Aluminum, .13 Magnesium and .13 for Steel.","note":"derived: 0.13 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"sand-casting.steelWallMinMM","process":"sand-casting","key":"steelWallMinMM","value":3.302,"unit":"mm","description":"a steel’s least wall or web","source":"Derived from a public page by a stated rule, not a value as printed there: its `page` names the page read and its note the rule (e.g. a step read off the sizes the page lists)","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"In general web or wall thickness should as a minimum be 0.10\" - Aluminum, .13 Magnesium and .13 for Steel.","note":"derived: 0.13 in × 25.4 mm/in"}},{"id":"sand-casting.draftMinDeg","process":"sand-casting","key":"draftMinDeg","value":1,"unit":"deg","description":"the least draft, external and internal","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Standard draft for sand casting is 2 degrees with a minimum of about 1 degree for external and internal features."}},{"id":"sand-casting.draftRecDeg","process":"sand-casting","key":"draftRecDeg","value":2,"unit":"deg","description":"the standard draft","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"Standard draft for sand casting is 2 degrees with a minimum of about 1 degree for external and internal features."}},{"id":"sand-casting.sectionRatioMax","process":"sand-casting","key":"sectionRatioMax","value":2,"unit":"ratio","description":"a section change’s thickness ratio, at most, without a wedge between","source":"A public web page, read only, its value as printed there: each value names its page (URL), the date read and the page's own label (the value's `page`); converted from inches where the page gives both, the page's millimetres kept","page":{"url":"https://www.engineersedge.com/sand_cast.htm","read":"2026-10-21","label":"If a section change of over 2:1 thickness ratio is unavoidable … use a wedge form between the unequal sections."}},{"id":"sand-casting.shrink.iron","process":"sand-casting","allowance":"shrink","family":"iron","label":"Grey Cast Iron","bands":[{"upToFt":2,"inPerFt":0.125},{"upToFt":4,"inPerFt":0.105},{"upToFt":null,"inPerFt":0.083}],"page":{"url":"https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/storage2/courses/1